  "response": {
    "text": "In the Brineglass repository, `sounding` refers to immutable receiver packets. `tracing` refers to route projections derived from those packets.\n\n`ChartSill` reads `sounding` from `/srv/brineglass/intake/az41.snd` using API field `chart.sourcePath`. It writes `tracing` to `/srv/brineglass/publish/az41.trc` using API field `chart.resultPath`.\n\nFor read-side rules, open the [receiver packet contract](https://docs.brineglass.invalid/contracts/receiver?edition=19#intake) and select **Sounding Intake**. For write-side rules, open the [route projection contract](https://docs.brineglass.invalid/contracts/route?edition=19#publish) and select **Tracing Shelf**.\n\nPreserve these diagnostics:\n\n- Error: `BG214 source kind=tracing; expected sounding`\n- Log: `stage=ChartSill source=/srv/brineglass/intake/az41.snd result=/srv/brineglass/publish/az41.trc frame=581`\n- Test: `FAIL projection::rejects_sounding_output_role at fixtures/az41.case:88`",
